flowchart TB
  accTitle: Push and pull move the same data with different request initiators
  accDescr: For push, A initiates a request containing event data to B using a key issued by B. For pull, B initiates a request to A using a key issued by A, then A returns eligible event data to B. Each direction has independent configuration and filters.
  subgraph push["PUSH · A initiates"]
    direction LR
    PA["Instance A<br/>Push enabled toward B"] -->|"Request + event data<br/>Key issued by B"| PB["Instance B<br/>Receives the event"]
  end
  subgraph pull["PULL · B initiates"]
    direction LR
    RB["Instance B<br/>Pull enabled from A"] -->|"Request<br/>Key issued by A"| RA["Instance A<br/>Checks the account's access"]
    RA -->|"Event data in response"| RB
  end
  push ~~~ pull
  class PA,PB,RA,RB accent;
